.TH SDL_GetWindowPosition 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetWindowPosition \- Get the position of a window.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_video.h>
.PP
.BI "bool SDL_GetWindowPosition(SDL_Window *window, int *x, int *y);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is the current position of the window as last reported by the windowing system\[char46]
.PP
If you do not need the value for one of the positions a NULL may be passed in the
.BR x
or
.BR y
parameter\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I window
the window to query\[char46]
.TP
.I x
a pointer filled in with the x position of the window, may be NULL\[char46]
.TP
.I y
a pointer filled in with the y position of the window, may be NULL\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns true on success or false on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_SetWindowPosition (3)
